# Eval evidence: keep the VERDICT, drop the regenerable bulk (2026-08-02).
# An eval run writes ~135 MB per strand, of which ~2.6 MB is the evidence anyone reads.
# The graph dumps are pure engine output — recreate them by re-running the instrument named
# in the matching *-EVIDENCE.md (e.g. eval-results/2026-08-02/G10/g10-threshold-sweep.ps1).
eval-results/**/raw/**
!eval-results/**/raw/*.stats.json
eval-results/**/*.graphdump.json

# Screenshots from a UI drive are working artifacts. Checked 2026-08-02: of 466 PNGs under
# eval-results/, the 20 that an EVIDENCE.md actually links were already tracked and stay tracked
# (.gitignore does not untrack); not one of the 96 then-uncommitted PNGs was referenced by any
# doc. If a future evidence doc needs one, `git add -f` it. Curated product screenshots live in
# docs/screenshots/ and are unaffected by this rule.
eval-results/**/*.png
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/
.opencode/

# A conductor session launched from a subdirectory writes its own .conductor/ there
# (one appeared under src/DevContext.App/ on 2026-07-29 and carried a crash log into `git add -A`).
# The repo-root .conductor/ has its own .gitignore and deliberately tracks only REPORT.md;
# anything nested is a stray. Anchored so the root one is untouched.
/*/**/.conductor/

# Eval artifacts
_eval-dntsite/
_eval-dntsite-results/
devcontext-dnt.md
devcontext-feed.md
devcontext-output.json
eval/.eval-stamp.json

